{
  "requirement": "`FileEvidenceStorage::new` retains the root directory without touching the filesystem.\nThe store implements `Send` and `Sync`. Its `load` and `store` futures are `Send`.\n\n`Record`, `Dependency`, and `Fingerprint` support Serde when their type\nparameters do. `Criterion::Ok` is always serializable; its JSON value is\nalready in the record. Serialization bounds on node identities and edge labels\napply when using this helper.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/storage.rs` adequately cover each obligation of `requirements.sdk.filesystem-storage.interface`.\n\n- **`new` retains the root without touching the filesystem.**\n  - `fn[paths_are_injective_and_loading_missing_records_has_no_side_effects]` builds the store on a nonexistent root. Every `record_path` is asserted equal to `root.join(expected)`, which shows the root is kept. After all the loads, the test asserts `!root.exists()`.\n  - `fn[send_futures_create_missing_roots_and_nested_paths_without_shortening_keys]` asserts `!root.exists()` right after `new`, before any `store` call.\n- **`Send` and `Sync` on the store.** `fn[concurrent_readers_only_observe_complete_records_from_competing_writes]` shares an `Arc<FileEvidenceStorage>` with spawned threads inside `std::thread::scope`. That compiles only if the store is `Send + Sync`.\n- **`load` and `store` futures are `Send`.** `fn[send_futures_create_missing_roots_and_nested_paths_without_shortening_keys]` passes both `store.store(..)` and `store.load::<String, ()>(..)` through `fn send<T: Send>`, so the bound is enforced at compile time.\n- **Serde support for `Record`, `Dependency` and `Fingerprint`.**\n  - `fn[records_round_trip_and_malformed_or_incompatible_data_is_an_error]` stores and loads records and asserts that `version`, `dependencies` and `output` come back equal. The `record()` helper covers both `Dependency::Node` and `Dependency::OutgoingEdges`, each with a `Fingerprint`.\n  - The test also round-trips a non-unit edge label (`String`, with the non-ASCII value `\"tests/é\"`).\n- **Serde works when the type parameters do.** Loading with the incompatible parameters `u8` for the node identity or `u8` for the edge label yields `FileStorageError::Json`. This shows the serialization bounds on node identities and edge labels apply. `fn[consumer_delegates_evidence_storage_using_only_the_requested_nodes_path]` adds a round trip of a record keyed by a custom node type through `StoredGraph`.\n- **`Criterion::Ok` is serializable and its JSON value is already in the record.** This is a descriptive note about the helper, not a separate behavior. The tests exercise it through the `serde_json::Value` output, which round-trips and is compared by equality.\n\nI found no obligation without a test and no marking gap. The `{test}` references on these tests name the subject.",
  "references": "4fa7c0209cc8a47ded44aa43c8f5142920833c5dae546977ebf2d7b4b9910690",
